    "body": "Thanks for the detailed write-up, @magiccodelab. \n1. **Why auto-compaction triggers around ~256K tokens by default:**\n   Even on models with a 1M-token (`1,048,576`) context window, Antigravity CLI intentionally sets the default automatic compaction threshold to `256,000` tokens. Because agentic turns re-send the active conversation context on every step, compacting at ~256K balances multi-step reasoning quality, turn latency, and per-turn quota consumption (larger active windows consume significantly more quota on every subsequent turn). As noted in the forum thread you linked, user-selectable context window tiers above 256K are not available yet.\n\n2. **Why `/context` displays `1.0M`:**\n   `/context` currently reports the selected model's total underlying context capacity (`1,048,576` tokens) rather than the active `256,000`-token auto-compaction threshold. We agree that showing `1.0M` without surfacing where automatic compaction will trigger makes this look like an unexpected cap rather than a compaction threshold.\n\nWe're tracking both parts of this feedback: https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/issues/878 https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/issues/1245",
